.TH GBRVEC 1
.SH NAME
gbrvec \- turn a Gerber or drill file into vectors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gbrvec
.I file
.RI > file.vec
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Gbrvec
reads an RS-274X or Excellon file and writes what it draws as
.IR vec (5),
in mm, with a name record for each part (from TO.C, or TO.P by its
part).
It reads the format and units, the apertures C, R and O, aperture
macros with primitives 1, 4, 5, 20 and 21 and their arithmetic, draws,
flashes, arcs, regions and polarity; and Excellon tools and holes.
A region under a net attribute (TO.N) begins a zone of the net.
The file function of Gerber X2 (TF.FileFunction, as an attribute or in
a comment) gives the layer record, by KiCad's name of the layer (F.Cu,
In1.Cu, B.Cu, F.Mask, F.Silkscreen, Edge.Cuts, ...); a drill file is
the layer Drill.
It reads the Gerbers of other programs, to compare or to show them;
the boards of
.IR pcb (5)
have their vectors from
.IR pcbvec (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
gbrvec gerber/top.gbr > top.vec
.SH SEE ALSO
vec(5), vecps(1), pcbview(1), pcbvec(1)
